name:           incremental-computations
version:        0.2.0.0
synopsis:       A framework for coarse-grained self-adjusting (incremental) computations
description:    A library for coarse-grained self-adjusting computations: define
                computations as a DAG of typed, named steps wired to pluggable sources and
                sinks, and let the engine incrementally recompute only what changed when an
                input updates. State is tracked per definition in a columnar cache, so
                reruns after a small input change touch a small, targeted slice of the
                computation graph rather than the whole thing. Originally extracted from a
                commercial product built by medilyse GmbH; this fork rewrites the engine
                internals and narrows the public API down to what a library consumer
                actually needs. See the README for a worked example and the accompanying
                FUNARCH 2023 paper for the underlying architecture.
category:       Control
homepage:       https://github.com/tvh/haskell-computations#readme
bug-reports:    https://github.com/tvh/haskell-computations/issues
author:         medilyse GmbH, Freiburg, Germany (https://medilyse.org)
maintainer:     Timo von Holtz
copyright:      2010-2023 medilyse GmbH, 2026 Timo von Holtz
license:        BSD3
